-- title:
--   Universal property of the full group C*-algebra — every unitary representation, on a Hilbert space in any universe, extends to C*(G) onto the C*-algebra it generates
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group (with the discrete topology, `G : Type u`), $H$ a complex Hilbert space in an arbitrary universe (`H : Type v`), and $\rho : G \to \mathrm U(\mathscr B(H))$ a homomorphism into the unitary group of the bounded operators on $H$. Then there is a unital $*$-homomorphism $\varphi : C^*(G) \to \mathscr B(H)$ of complex algebras with $\varphi(g) = \rho(g)$ for every $g \in G$, where $C^*(G)$ is `FullGroupCStar G` and $g$ stands for its canonical unitary `FullGroupCStar.of g`; and the range of $\varphi$ is the $C^*$-subalgebra of $\mathscr B(H)$ generated by the $\rho(g)$, the closure of the $*$-subalgebra they generate.
--
--   The norm of `FullGroupCStar G` is defined as a supremum over representations on Hilbert spaces in the universe of $G$, and `FullGroupCStar.lift` already extends those. This statement asks the same for Hilbert spaces in every universe, which is the universal property by which Choi defines $C^*(F_2)$ (Pacific J. Math. 87 (1980), p. 41, a $C^*$-algebra generated by a universal family of unitaries).
-- source:
--   Choi, M. D., The full C*-algebra of the free group on two generators, Pacific J. Math. 87 (1980) 41–48, https://doi.org/10.2140/pjm.1980.87.41, p. 41, the universal property defining C*(F_2) (Introduction, Definition)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FullGroupCStar

universe u v

namespace FullGroupCStar

theorem exists_starAlgHom_comp_of_eq_and_range_eq {G : Type u} [Group G] (H : Type v)
    [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]
    (ρ : G →* unitary (H →L[ℂ] H)) :
    ∃ φ : FullGroupCStar G →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H), (∀ g : G, φ (of g) = ρ g) ∧
      φ.range = (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range fun g : G => (ρ g : H →L[ℂ] H))).topologicalClosure := by
  sorry

end FullGroupCStar
